+# Zero-Admin Guide — 100% Autonomous Landing Handbook
+
+> **Policy:** Admin manual effort budget **≤ 0.01%** (AGENTS.md §2.1).
+> **Audience:** every PR submitter — local, cloud, web-AI, or external contributors.
+> **Promise:** if your PR satisfies the checklist in §5, it lands **with zero human hands involved** — and every prior failure class has a guard that catches it before an admin would ever look at it.
+
+## 1. Why human manual merging is eliminated by design
+
+Human "review-and-click-merge" is not accelerated in this federation — it is **removed from the critical path**. The design replaces each function a human reviewer used to serve with a deterministic, evidence-producing mechanism:
+
+| Human-reviewer function | Replaced by | Where enforced |
+|---|---|---|
+| "Is this contributor allowed?" | Zero-credential pathways — fork+PR needs no permission at all | AGENTS.md §2.1 (Pathways 1–3) |
+| "Does this PR respect scope?" | Touching-Files scope gate + Boundary Sanitization Guard | pipeline.yml `boundary_sanitization_guard` (#107) |
+| "Is this duplicate work?" | Anti-Duplicate PR Guard (whole-token `#N` matching) | pipeline.yml `duplicate_pr_guard` (U4) |
+| "Does it reference a real task?" | Issue Reference Guard | pipeline.yml `issue_reference_guard` |
+| "Is the code quality acceptable?" | Python 3.10–3.13 matrix + Tower TS verification + self-tests | pipeline.yml `test-matrix`, `mcp_tower` |
+| "Any secrets leaked?" | Gitleaks full-history scan | pipeline.yml `secrets-scan` |
+| "Is the PR well-formed?" | CI Guardian AI evaluation (template, scope, evidence, security) | docs/GUARDIAN_EVALUATION.md |
+| "Is the branch current?" | Stale-Base Guard + local pre-push hook freshness check | pipeline.yml `stale_base_guard` (#161) |
+| "May this rewrite history?" | Zero-Force-Push: local poka-yoke + server-side pre-receive rejection | docs/INGRESS_SECURITY_POLICY.md |
+| "Merge it and close the task." | Merge Gate: squash-merge with title/body preservation + close-keyword propagation + head-branch auto-deletion | landing.yml; Command Router post-merge cleanup |
+
+Two structural facts make the budget ≤ 0.01% rather than merely small:
+
+1. **Shift-left on the free public runtime.** Everything provable in public (guards, matrix, typecheck, secret scan, boundary audit, AI evaluation) runs on the *public* repo's unlimited free Actions minutes; the private repo keeps only what requires private context (docs/OPS_ACTIONS_QUOTA_RUNBOOK.md). Admin attention is never spent on work that failed cheaply and early.
+2. **Fail-closed, evidence-first doctrine (U2).** Automation never claims `PASS` without reproducible evidence, and never silently skips a check. The output of every gate is machine-readable, so the next machine (the gate, the bridge, the coder agent) can consume it without a human translating.
+
+## 2. CI Guardian — autonomous verification criteria
+
+The CI Guardian (AI PR evaluator, contract `guardian-evaluation/1`) is specified in `docs/GUARDIAN_EVALUATION.md` — that document is the SSOT for **how** a verdict is derived. Summary of the autonomous criteria:
+
+- **Four weighted check categories:** `template_adherence` (20), `scope_boundary` (25), `test_evidence` (30), `security_scan` (25).
+- **Verdicts:** `PASS` (all categories pass and `score.overall ≥ threshold`), `HOLD` (any single fail — the PR receives an additive `HOLD_AND_FIX` healing list), `REJECT` (non-healable violation).
+- **Autonomous merge eligibility:** `eligible = (verdict == PASS) AND (score.overall ≥ threshold) AND (no security_scan fail)`. An eligible PR **may be landed by merge automation with no human in the loop**.
+- **Determinism:** a re-run on the same head SHA produces byte-identical output; every verdict cites its fired rules verbatim so it is re-derivable from the check list alone (U2).
+- **Healing loop:** every HOLD emits `healing_instructions`, one concrete step per failed criterion; items marked `automatable: true` are executable by a coder agent **without human judgement** — that is the mechanism that keeps humans out of the fix loop, too.
+
+## 3. Merge Gate semantics (what actually lands your PR)
+
+The gate (`landing.yml`) is the only landing authority on `main`:
+
+1. **Squash-only landing** with a deterministic message: subject = `<PR title> (#<PR number>)`, body = the PR description.
+2. **Closing-keyword propagation (#165 doctrine):** GitHub processes `Closes #N` from the **final squash commit message only** — so put `Closes #N` in the **PR title and body** (both survive into the squash message). A keyword that only exists in a commit on your branch will not close the task issue.
+3. **File-set parity:** the merge commit's file set must equal the PR's reviewed diff — no surprise content.
+4. **Freshness:** a PR whose branch is behind `main` is rejected (⏳ Stale-Base Guard at CI time; the same rule locally via `.githooks/pre-push`). Rebase/merge-sync and the gate re-evaluates.
+5. **Zero-Force-Push:** force-pushes are rejected locally by the pre-push hook and server-side by pre-receive protection. Re-push a fixed branch as a fast-forward only.
+6. **Post-merge cleanup:** the Command Router deletes the PR head branch and verifies task-issue closure autonomously.
+
+## 4. When admin attention IS required (the honest 0.01%)
+
+Zero-Admin does not mean zero humans. Admin involvement is reserved for what is **constitucionally outside agent authority** (AGENTS.md §1.3/§4/§6):
+
+- Issues carrying an **ADMIN_DECISION gate** (e.g. governance/boundary decisions — the boundary itself is admin-owned).
+- Repository-level settings that no credential agent may change (branch protection, org secrets, app installs).
+- Escalations for **hard blockers**: missing credentials, destructive/irreversible operations, contradictory instructions (U10).
+
+Everything else — verification, fixing, merging, closing, cleaning up — is designed to complete without a human.
+
+## 5. Submitter checklist for 100% autonomous auto-merge
+
+Work through this list **before opening the PR**; each unchecked item is a documented auto-merge killer:
+
+- [ ] **Task selection:** issue is open and claimable (no `status:claimed`/`status:in-progress`/`state:seq-hold`/`blocked-by-upstream`/`mirror:private` label, no ADMIN_DECISION gate).
+- [ ] **Claim first:** post a claim comment; if the board assigns `status:claimed`, keep it. No competing PR exists for the issue (U4 preflight — check open PRs).
+- [ ] **One issue = one PR, anywhere in the federation.** Never open a manual PR on the private repo for public-boundary work (#155 Public-First SSOT).
+- [ ] **Branch naming:** `^(feat|fix|docs|chore|test|refactor|perf|bridge|group|contributor|hotfix|release|agent)/<slug>` — bot branches are auto-allowed.
+- [ ] **Scope:** only the issue's declared Touching Files (plus what the governing issue/its work orders explicitly justify — record the justification in the PR body).
+- [ ] **Reference the task:** PR title **and** body contain `#<issue>`; include `Closes #<issue>` in the title or body so the squash message carries the close keyword (#165 doctrine).
+- [ ] **Evidence in the body:** the commands you ran and their real results (tier outputs, self-tests, exit codes). No `PASS` without evidence (U2).
+- [ ] **Fresh base:** branch is rebased/merged onto the current `main` tip (⏳ Stale-Base Guard rejects `behind > 0`).
+- [ ] **Green locally:** run the 3-tier verification — `python scripts/agents/continuous_agent_loop.py --verify-only` (8 tiers) — plus any suite your change touches (e.g. `npm run test:tower-ci` for Tower work, `sh .githooks/pre-push --self-test` for hook work).
+- [ ] **No secrets, no machine paths:** no credentials, no absolute host paths in source (`C:\`, `/Users/...`), no boundary-drift files.
+- [ ] **Small, atomic diff:** one logical change; file-set matches the PR description exactly.
+- [ ] **Never force-push.** Fix forward with fast-forward pushes.
+
+A PR that satisfies this checklist has historically landed **without any admin action** — the guards + CI Guardian + gate complete the loop: verify → hold-and-fix (autonomously healable) → merge → close issue → delete branch.
